? Use `pi install git:github.com/cv/pit@v0.36.4` instead; package updates won't move a pinned install.\\n \\n For a one-session trial or a project-only install, see [installation options](docs/configuration.md#installation-scope). Pit is distributed from GitHub, not npm; [releases](https://github.com/cv/pit/releases) and the [changelog](CHANGELOG.md) cover what's new.\\n \\ndiff --git a/docs/durable.md b/docs/durable.md\\nindex dc4142f..cc0d74e 100644\\n--- a/docs/durable.md\\n+++ b/docs/durable.md\\n@@ -84,6 +84,8 @@ Existing conversations keep their history: earlier calls to a tool that is no lo\\n \\n Results are plain text for the model plus the same JSON `details` Pi's renderers read: the value, progress, traces, timings, and saved-function changes. Command output streams through `output()` while a call runs. A failed call returns an error result whose text is the root error, as on Pi.\\n \\n+The `typescript` tool also carries a `present` field for hosts that show tool calls in a log, such as [pi-action's workflow log](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/main/docs/extensions.md#show-tool-calls-in-the-workflow-log). pi-durable ignores it. `present.call(args)` gives the call's title, the label from the `// @pit:` header or the `label` argument, and a body: the program without the header, then `params` as JSON, `functionId`, and `saveOnly`. `present.result(args, result)` gives a summary, the functions the program injected such as `workspace.read · git.status` (`saved <name>` for `saveOnly`, the error's first line on failure), and a body: the returned value with string fields as they are and other values as indented JSON, or the error.\\n+\\n ## What doesn't\\n \\n These throw a `PitDurableUnavailableError` whose message names the global, such as `commands.list is unavailable on pi-durable hosts: the host has no slash commands`:\\ndiff --git a/package-lock.json b/package-lock.json\\nindex ad8212d..32c79fc 100644\\n--- a/package-lock.json\\n+++ b/package-lock.json\\n@@ -1,12 +1,12 @@\\n {\\n   \\\"name\\\": \\\"pit\\\",\\n-  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.3\\\",\\n+  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.4\\\",\\n   \\\"lockfileVersion\\\": 3,\\n   \\\"requires\\\": true,\\n   \\\"packages\\\": {\\n     \\\"\\\": {\\n       \\\"name\\\": \\\"pit\\\",\\n-      \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.3\\\",\\n+      \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.4\\\",\\n       \\\"license\\\": \\\"MIT\\\",\\n       \\\"dependencies\\\": {\\n         \\\"@earendil-works/pi-codemode\\\": \\\"1.5.0\\\",\\ndiff --git a/package.json b/package.json\\nindex d4e3b5e..dd149eb 100644\\n--- a/package.json\\n+++ b/package.json\\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\\n {\\n   \\\"name\\\": \\\"pit\\\",\\n-  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.3\\\",\\n+  \\\"version\\\": \\\"0.36.4\\\",\\n   \\\"description\\\": \\\"A single, dependency-injected TypeScript tool for Pi\\\",\\n   \\\"type\\\": \\\"module\\\",\\n   \\\"files\\\": [\\ndiff --git a/src/durable/tool.ts b/src/durable/tool.ts\\nindex 53ef450..ece5ff5 100644\\n--- a/src/durable/tool.ts\\n+++ b/src/durable/tool.ts\\n@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@ import {\\n   unavailableNamespace,\\n } from \\\"./host.js\\\";\\n import { createDurableImageCollector } from \\\"./images.js\\\";\\n+import { TYPESCRIPT_PRESENTATION, type ToolPresentation } from \\\"./present.js\\\";\\n import { DurableQuestions, type QuestionPosted } from \\\"./questions.js\\\";\\n import { createDurableSessionHandler } from \\\"./session.js\\\";\\n import {\\n@@ -380,9 +381,11 @@ function takeLoadWarnings(functions: ConversationFunctions, log: PitDurableLog |\\n /** Pit's `typescript` tool as a pi-durable tool registration. */\\n export function createDurableTypeScriptTool(\\n   services: DurableToolServices,\\n-): ToolRegistration<typeof DURABLE_TOOL_PARAMETERS> {\\n+): ToolRegistration<typeof DURABLE_TOOL_PARAMETERS> & { present: ToolPresentation } {\\n   return {\\n     name: \\\"typescript\\\",\\n+    // How hosts such as pi-action show the calls in their logs; pi-durable ignores it.\\n+    present: TYPESCRIPT_PRESENTATION,\\n     description: `${createToolDescription(LIMITS.result.maxBytes)}\\\\n${HOST_NOTES}`,\\n     parameters: DURABLE_TOOL_PARAMETERS,\\n     // The Harness validates the prepared arguments against the parameters afterwards.\\n\",\"diffTruncated\":false,\"stagedDiff\":\"\",\"stagedDiffTruncated\":false,\"recentCommits\":\"3163c2d ci: run pi-action v2.5.1 with pit 0.36.3\\nf2ddcec chore(release): v0.36.3\\n6d7f6d5 fix(input): decode a params string sent as a JSON string literal\\n61457eb chore(release): v0.36.2\\ncfb2440 feat(durable): attach images from workspace.viewImage and nested tools (#365)\"}",
